IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P3-section-3: the gate that every provision of Articles 16 to 27 (Chapter III, Section 3) passes through.
-- It is infrastructure, not a provision: it takes the keel's answers (seams S13, S14 and S15 of PLAN.md section 4) and says, for one
-- provision of this part, whether the provision applies to the AI system on the date asked.
--
--   1. Art 113 (with Art 111(2)): the group `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` applies from a date that depends on the route to high-risk,
--      and Art 111(2) saves a legacy system that has not been significantly changed. Before that: `Section 3 not applicable on the date asked`.
--   2. Art 2(2) (S14): for a system high-risk under Article 6(1) related to products of Section B of Annex I, "only Article 6(1), Article 60a
--      and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply", so none of Articles 16 to 27 does: `Section 3 cut off by Article 2(2)`.
--   3. Art 2(13) (S15): for a system high-risk under Article 6(1), the application of specific requirements or obligations laid down in
--      Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25 "may be limited, where and to the extent that" Section A legislation gives equivalent protection and the
--      overall level of protection is not reduced. Which obligations, and to what extent, is for the Commission's delegated acts under
--      Article 97, which are not among the sources: `Section 3 may be limited under Article 2(13)`.
--   4. Otherwise: `Section 3 applies`.
-- How a provision uses the answer (every decision function of this part does the same):
--   shut by 1 or 3      -> NOTHING  (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording, or points outside the text)
--   cut off by 2        -> JUST FALSE (FALSE-kind: the flat "only ... shall apply" of Art 2(2))
--   open                -> the provision's own answer.
-- A regulative rule of this part answers FULFILLED when the gate is shut or cuts the provision off (nothing is owed).

§ `The facts a part needs besides the AI system: Section B of Annex I and Article 2(13)`

-- The three facts about the system that Art 2(2) and Art 2(13) turn on and that the core's `AI system` does not carry. A seat builds this record
-- inside the question from three plain answers. The Article 2(2) input "requirements integrated in the Union harmonisation legislation" is
-- irrelevant to Articles 16 to 27 (it only governs Articles 57 to 59), so the gate passes FALSE for it.
DECLARE `Section 3 circumstances` HAS
    `related to Section B products`                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- the high-risk AI system is related to products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I
    `Section A equivalent protection`                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- Art 2(13)(a): Section A legislation lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection
    `no reduction of the overall level of protection`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- Art 2(13)(b): such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation

§ `The four answers of the gate`

DECLARE `Section 3 gate result` IS ONE OF
    `Section 3 not applicable on the date asked`
    `Section 3 cut off by Article 2(2)`
    `Section 3 may be limited under Article 2(13)`
    `Section 3 applies`

§ `The gate`

-- `the provision` is the Article the caller implements: number 16 to 27, letter "", paragraph 0 (the keel's `Article reference`).
-- Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 give no date to a system that is not high-risk (route neither), so the gate is shut for it.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provision` IS AN `Article reference`
GIVETH A `Section 3 gate result`
`Section 3 gate` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`) (`the AI system`'s `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`))
    THEN `Section 3 not applicable on the date asked`
    ELSE IF (`Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) (`the circumstances`'s `related to Section B products`) FALSE `the provision`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN `Section 3 cut off by Article 2(2)`
         ELSE IF (`Art 2(13) the application of the requirement or obligation may be limited` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) `the provision` (`the circumstances`'s `Section A equivalent protection`) (`the circumstances`'s `no reduction of the overall level of protection`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN `Section 3 may be limited under Article 2(13)`
              ELSE `Section 3 applies`

-- What a decision function answers when the gate is not open (the open case is the provision's own answer).
GIVEN `the gate` IS A `Section 3 gate result`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the gate`
    WHEN `Section 3 cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Art 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply"
    WHEN `Section 3 not applicable on the date asked` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 113(c) gives Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 a date of application, and Art 111(2) saves a legacy system
    WHEN `Section 3 may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "may be limited, where and to the extent that"; the delegated acts under Article 97 specify what
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- the gate is open: the caller answers; this arm is never reached by a caller that tests `Section 3 applies` first

-- Does a regulative rule of this part bind? Only when the gate is open: a shut gate or a provision cut off by Art 2(2) owes nothing.
GIVEN `the gate` IS A `Section 3 gate result`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Section 3 the gate is open` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the gate`
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
